    "title": "Local Families Invited to Children's Duck Exploration Event at Mason Regional Park - NewsBreak",
    "text": "55 minutes ago Families with children ages 3 to 6 can attend the 'Little Explorers: Ducks!' event at Mason Regional Park in Irvine. OC Park naturalists will lead a story time and a short hike about ducks. Children under 18 must be with a parent or guardian.\nRegistration is required, and a waiver must be signed at the event. The event is at 18712 University Drive. Parking costs $5 per car in Lot C. Parking is limited, so carpooling is recommended.\nParticipants should bring water, wear closed-toed shoes, and use sun protection. Group sizes are limited for safety. The event may be canceled due to weather or trail conditions. For questions or group registration, contact the event organizers by email.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
